@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.1870 = private unnamed_addr constant [2092 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `return {value}` statements in functions that also contain `yield`\0Aor `yield from` statements.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUsing `return {value}` in a generator function was syntactically invalid in\0APython 2. In Python 3 `return {value}` _can_ be used in a generator; however,\0Athe combination of `yield` and `return` can lead to confusing behavior, as\0Athe `return` statement will cause the generator to raise `StopIteration`\0Awith the value provided, rather than returning the value to the caller.\0A\0AFor example, given:\0A```python\0Afrom collections.abc import Iterable\0Afrom pathlib import Path\0A\0A\0Adef get_file_paths(file_types: Iterable[str] | None = None) -> Iterable[Path]:\0A    dir_path = Path(\22.\22)\0A    if file_types is None:\0A        return dir_path.glob(\22*\22)\0A\0A    for file_type in file_types:\0A        yield from dir_path.glob(f\22*.{file_type}\22)\0A```\0A\0AReaders might assume that `get_file_paths()` would return an iterable of\0A`Path` objects in the directory; in reality, though, `list(get_file_paths())`\0Aevaluates to `[]`, since the `return` statement causes the generator to raise\0A`StopIteration` with the value `dir_path.glob(\22*\22)`:\0A\0A```shell\0A>>> list(get_file_paths(file_types=[\22cfg\22, \22toml\22]))\0A[PosixPath('setup.cfg'), PosixPath('pyproject.toml')]\0A>>> list(get_file_paths())\0A[]\0A```\0A\0AFor intentional uses of `return` in a generator, consider suppressing this\0Adiagnostic.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom collections.abc import Iterable\0Afrom pathlib import Path\0A\0A\0Adef get_file_paths(file_types: Iterable[str] | None = None) -> Iterable[Path]:\0A    dir_path = Path(\22.\22)\0A    if file_types is None:\0A        return dir_path.glob(\22*\22)\0A\0A    for file_type in file_types:\0A        yield from dir_path.glob(f\22*.{file_type}\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom collections.abc import Iterable\0Afrom pathlib import Path\0A\0A\0Adef get_file_paths(file_types: Iterable[str] | None = None) -> Iterable[Path]:\0A    dir_path = Path(\22.\22)\0A    if file_types is None:\0A        yield from dir_path.glob(\22*\22)\0A    else:\0A        for file_type in file_types:\0A            yield from dir_path.glob(f\22*.{file_type}\22)\0A```\0A", align 1
