@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.1874 = private unnamed_addr constant [563 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the use of `exclude` in Django `ModelForm` classes.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf a `ModelForm` includes the `exclude` attribute, any new field that\0Ais added to the model will automatically be exposed for modification.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom django.forms import ModelForm\0A\0A\0Aclass PostForm(ModelForm):\0A    class Meta:\0A        model = Post\0A        exclude = [\22author\22]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom django.forms import ModelForm\0A\0A\0Aclass PostForm(ModelForm):\0A    class Meta:\0A        model = Post\0A        fields = [\22title\22, \22content\22]\0A```\0A", align 1
