@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.1907 = private unnamed_addr constant [384 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for redundant definitions of `__str__` or `__repr__` in stubs.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ADefining `__str__` or `__repr__` in a stub is almost always redundant,\0Aas the signatures are almost always identical to those of the default\0Aequivalent, `object.__str__` and `object.__repr__`, respectively.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```pyi\0Aclass Foo:\0A    def __repr__(self) -> str: ...\0A```\0A", align 1
