@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.1926 = private unnamed_addr constant [548 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the presence of unused arguments in function definitions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAn argument that is defined but not used is likely a mistake, and should\0Abe removed to avoid confusion.\0A\0AIf a variable is intentionally defined-but-not-used, it should be\0Aprefixed with an underscore, or some other value that adheres to the\0A[`lint.dummy-variable-rgx`] pattern.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef foo(bar, baz):\0A    return bar * 2\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef foo(bar):\0A    return bar * 2\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.dummy-variable-rgx`\0A", align 1
