@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2082 = private unnamed_addr constant [31 x i8] c"unnecessary-multiline-docstring", align 1
@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2083 = private unnamed_addr constant [823 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for single-line docstrings that are broken across multiple lines.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 257] recommends that docstrings that _can_ fit on one line should be\0Aformatted on a single line, for consistency and readability.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef average(values: list[float]) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22\0A    Return the mean of the given values.\0A    \22\22\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef average(values: list[float]) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Return the mean of the given values.\22\22\22\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThe fix is marked as unsafe because it could affect tools that parse docstrings,\0Adocumentation generators, or custom introspection utilities that rely on\0Aspecific docstring formatting.\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A\0A[PEP 257]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/\0A", align 1
