@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2093 = private unnamed_addr constant [466 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for common mistakes when using mock objects.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `mock` module exposes an assertion API that can be used to verify that\0Amock objects undergo expected interactions. This rule checks for common\0Amistakes when using this API.\0A\0AFor example, it checks for mock attribute accesses that should be replaced\0Awith mock method calls.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Amy_mock.assert_called\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Amy_mock.assert_called()\0A```\0A", align 1
