@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2211 = private unnamed_addr constant [649 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for form feed characters preceded by either a space or a tab.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[The language reference][lexical-analysis-indentation] states:\0A\0A> A formfeed character may be present at the start of the line;\0A> it will be ignored for the indentation calculations above.\0A> Formfeed characters occurring elsewhere in the leading whitespace\0A> have an undefined effect (for instance, they may reset the space count to zero).\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aif foo():\\n    \\fbar()\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aif foo():\\n    bar()\0A```\0A\0A[lexical-analysis-indentation]: https://docs.python.org/3/reference/lexical_analysis.html#indentation\0A", align 1
